05:33.180 --> 05:36.360
Try and suggest, maybe not this (laughs)

05:36.360 --> 05:38.340
but maybe there's a bug that someone's identified

05:38.340 --> 05:40.200
and I volunteer to fix it.

05:40.200 --> 05:42.150
I would need to clone the repository.

05:42.150 --> 05:43.620
Whether I'm just messing around

05:43.620 --> 05:46.530
and breaking things and playing and changing colors,

05:46.530 --> 05:48.540
whether I'm trying to understand how something works

05:48.540 --> 05:52.980
or whether I wanna make contributions, I need to clone.

05:52.980 --> 05:56.190
So that command git clone, it's pretty simple.

05:56.190 --> 05:57.990
Just git clone and then a URL.

05:57.990 --> 06:00.930
Make sure you're not in a Git repository when you run it

06:00.930 --> 06:03.270
because it creates, well, it creates a folder,

06:03.270 --> 06:05.730
